# Normalise line endings in the repository and on every checkout.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone receives CRLF and two things break that are
# easy to misread as product faults: assertions that read workflow or script
# text fail only on Windows, and a shell script written with CRLF is rejected
# by the kernel with a confusing "bad interpreter" error.
#
# Generated artifacts decide their own line endings at runtime — the PowerShell
# shim is emitted with CRLF by the installer, which is unaffected by this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.exe binary
*.obj binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
